Janis Papanagnou wrote:
> BanMido wrote:
>
>> I did not mention this earlier, I am at 'Skilled' level in both long
>> sword and two weapon fighting. So, I was basically planning to become
>> 'Expert' in both and duel wield two long swords/katanas. So should I
>> abandon longsword skill development and get Grayswandir?
>
> (I suppose you know that Samurai can get only Basic in sabres?)

Because skill slots are limited and missile combat is so valuable it is
worth looking at the possibilities and establishing a tentative strategy
for skill slots.  Expert skill is very expensive so an earlier character
might consider it a trap designed to waste resources.  As samurais are
bow users it becomes worth advancing it somewhere in the middle game.  I
like to save skill slots for that.  The skill slot strategy may be
ignored for point survival but having one at all gives good context.  My
samurai one goes like this -

The order goes something like, dagger to basic (max), long sword to
skilled, two weapon to basic, two weapon to skilled, bow to skilled,
saber to basic (max), bow to expert (max), long sword to expert (max),
two weapon to expert (max), with spells, polearms or other items mixed
in as appropriate.

> Grayswandir is very nice to have. Two-weaponing it with a katana would
> probably be my choice. But Snickersnee two-weaponed with another katana
> or with a silver sabre is nothing to spit on, to say the least.
>
>> So, Excalibur will generally be better as I progress, right?
>
> Well, I find the searching property to be worth having Excalibur; helps
> avoiding a couple traps that may annoy you. Level drain resistance is
> not too important, but depends on the cloak you wear; if you have MC3
> you don't need the sword, if you have MC2 you need a bit more care, but
> that's it.

Any of Snickersnee, Excalibur or Grayswandir are ascendable artifact
weapons.  I think either Excalibur or Grayswandir beat Snickersnee, as
do the Banes.  Excalibur is never given as a sac gift, just dipping and
crowning so it doesn't interfere with a decision to do a sac fast or to
continue a sac fest.  Do dozens or hundreds of post-clover sacs and
collect a few artifacts.  If you get Grayswandir or a Bane you're lucky.
I still explore with Excalibur whenever I have it.


